这非常罕见。

1111
00:50:43.680 --> 00:50:45.920
We only did this a couple of times on our set.
我们在片场只拍过几次这样的戏。

1112
00:50:46.060 --> 00:50:47.240
But here's what happened.
但事情是这样的。

1113
00:50:47.980 --> 00:50:53.840
Randall told me that he requested that we be able to hear one another.
兰德尔告诉我，他要求我们能够听到彼此的声音。

1114
00:50:54.020 --> 00:50:55.220
But not just that.
不仅如此。

1115
00:50:55.380 --> 00:50:58.560
He wanted to shoot both sides of the conversation at the same time.
他想同时拍摄对话的双方。

1116
00:50:58.740 --> 00:51:03.160
And this was really complicated because the Stanford set was in one building.
这非常复杂，因为斯坦福的片场在一栋楼里。

1117
00:51:03.160 --> 00:51:05.340
And then there was a huge parking lot.
中间隔着一个巨大的停车场。

1118
00:51:05.520 --> 00:51:07.880
And then the Scranton set was in another building.
而斯克兰顿的片场在另一栋楼里。

1119
00:51:07.880 --> 00:51:15.960
And he said he thinks that it was his inexperience as a director that led him to making this.
他说他认为正是他作为导演的经验不足，才让他提出了这个要求。

1120
00:51:15.960 --> 00:51:20.660
What he realizes now was, like, a very bold, complicated requeSt.
他现在意识到，这在当时是一个非常大胆且复杂的要求。

1121
00:51:21.540 --> 00:51:24.000
Logistically, this was very hard to do.
从后勤角度来看，这非常难实现。

1122
00:51:24.120 --> 00:51:25.620
And he didn't realize that.
但他当时并没有意识到这一点。

1123
00:51:26.080 --> 00:51:31.680
No, he was like, hey, listen, when we do that scene with Jim and Pam, I'm going to want to be able to, like, have a camera on each of them.
不，他当时就像是说，嘿，听着，当我们拍吉姆和帕姆那场戏时，我想在他们每个人身上都架一台摄像机。

1124
00:51:31.680 --> 00:51:34.680
And I want them to be able to hear each other on the phone.
而且我希望他们能通过电话听到对方的声音。

1125
00:51:35.920 --> 00:51:41.000
And he says now, looking back, he realizes what an insane request that was.
他现在说，回过头来看，他意识到那是一个多么疯狂的要求。

1126
00:51:41.100 --> 00:51:42.580
Because here's what had to happen.
因为必须得这样做。

1127
00:51:43.300 --> 00:51:46.300
Kent told me that NBC Universal IT came out.
肯特告诉我，NBC环球的IT部门出动了。

1128
00:51:46.500 --> 00:51:52.740
