1470
01:10:58.040 --> 01:11:04.460
And I think there, there was a traditional and very, very likely correct, but a traditional
我觉得当时有一种传统的，而且很可能非常正确的，但确实是传统的

1471
01:11:05.420 --> 01:11:10.320
view of you don't, we don't do one-off experiments on this show.
观点，就是我们不能，我们不能在这个节目里做一次性的实验。

1472
01:11:10.480 --> 01:11:11.740
You know, we tell the story.
你知道，我们讲的是故事。

1473
01:11:11.780 --> 01:11:15.260
And there's an A and a B and a C story and you've got to stick to that.
有A线、B线和C线故事，你必须坚持那样做。

1474
01:11:15.360 --> 01:11:15.580
Yeah.
是的。

1475
01:11:15.660 --> 01:11:18.880
It wasn't experimental and it did work by and large the show.
它不是实验性的，而且总的来说，这个节目确实很成功。

1476
01:11:19.040 --> 01:11:22.640
So I can't really argue, but yeah, I, I'm sort of experimental like you.
所以我没法反驳，但确实，我，我和你一样，有点喜欢实验性。

1477
01:11:22.680 --> 01:11:23.900
I like that kind of thing.
我喜欢那种东西。

1478
01:11:24.060 --> 01:11:26.440
I feel like community did things like that.
我觉得《废柴联盟》就做过那种事。

1479
01:11:26.640 --> 01:11:27.140
Yes.
没错。

1480
01:11:27.400 --> 01:11:28.040
Every episode.
每一集都是。

1481
01:11:28.300 --> 01:11:29.000
They could get away with that.
他们能那样做而不受影响。

1482
01:11:29.100 --> 01:11:30.340
Really wild one-offs.
非常疯狂的一次性尝试。

1483
01:11:30.540 --> 01:11:32.440
And, and I definitely, I'm with you, Rain.
而且，而且我绝对支持你，雷恩。

1484
01:11:32.480 --> 01:11:37.780
I pitched a few times that, that we would follow characters home and I was, you know, told pretty
我提议过几次，我们可以跟着角色回家，但我被，你知道，很快就告知了，

1485
01:11:37.780 --> 01:11:39.120
quickly, but it's the office.
但这是《办公室》。

1486
01:11:39.120 --> 01:11:40.500
It's called the office.
剧名就叫《办公室》。

1487
01:11:40.500 --> 01:11:42.880
We're not going other places.
我们不能去别的地方。

1488
01:11:43.320 --> 01:11:49.440
But in this episode, and here's steering us back, we go to Dwight's beet farm.
但在这一集里，把话题拉回来，我们去了德怀特的甜菜农场。

1489
01:11:49.440 --> 01:11:58.320
So we do, we do go home with a character and is, is this, what time is this?
所以我们确实，我们确实跟着角色回家了，这是，这是什么时候？

1490
01:11:58.420 --> 01:11:59.340
Was this the first time?
这是第一次吗？

1491
01:11:59.460 --> 01:12:02.100
Second time we went to Dwight's farm and was this the first time?
我们第二次去德怀特的农场，这是第一次吗？

1492
01:12:02.100 --> 01:12:03.440
I knew it was the, gotta be the first time.
我知道这，肯定是第一次。

1493
01:12:03.600 --> 01:12:05.360
And was it the production of Moe's?
那是莫斯（Mose）的制作吗？

1494
01:12:05.460 --> 01:12:07.380
Was this the first time with Moe's?
这是第一次有莫斯吗？

1495
01:12:07.420 --> 01:12:07.920
Yeah.
是的。

1496
01:12:08.280 --> 01:12:08.600
Yes.
是的。

1497
01:12:09.120 --> 01:12:09.440
Yes.
是的。

1498
01:12:09.620 --> 01:12:11.680
This episode was history then.
那这一集就是历史性的了。

1499
01:12:12.580 --> 01:12:12.900
Yes.
是的。

1500
01:12:13.100 --> 01:12:14.440
So, well, let's see.
好吧，让我们看看。

1501
01:12:14.440 --> 01:12:19.520
Well, let me just say as a writer who obsessed about things like this, that the audience didn't
好吧，作为一名对这类细节极其执着的编剧，我得说，观众其实根本

1502
01:12:19.520 --> 01:12:26.360
give a shit about at the end of the day, which was how would the documentarians be or not
不在乎这些，比如纪录片摄制组到底能不能

1503
01:12:26.360 --> 01:12:28.360
be allowed to follow certain things?
被允许去跟拍某些事情？

1504
01:12:28.560 --> 01:12:33.460
You know, we would always say you'd never see Jim and Pam's bedroom because they would
你知道，我们总说你永远不会看到吉姆和帕姆的卧室，因为他们

1505
01:12:33.460 --> 01:12:35.240
never invite the cameras there.
绝不会邀请摄像机进去。

1506
01:12:35.420 --> 01:12:36.040
Are you crazy?
你疯了吗？

1507
01:12:37.580 --> 01:12:41.640
Whereas Dwight's beet farm, the camera coup would be very interested.
但如果是德怀特的甜菜农场，摄制组肯定会非常感兴趣。

1508
01:12:41.640 --> 01:12:45.460
It's very relevant to this new employee, Ryan's journey at Thunder Mifflin.
这对新员工瑞安在邓德米福林公司的旅程非常重要。

1509
01:12:45.600 --> 01:12:50.080
It's very relevant to this major personality at Thunder Mifflin, Dwight.
这对邓德米福林公司的重要人物德怀特来说也非常重要。

1510
01:12:50.260 --> 01:12:51.920
It's fundamental to his nature.
这是他本性中不可或缺的一部分。

1511
01:12:52.120 --> 01:12:53.380
We've heard about it a lot.
我们已经听过很多次了。

1512
01:12:53.600 --> 01:13:01.000
He would be extremely eager to show his beet farm, especially as part of a work-related
他会非常渴望展示他的甜菜农场，尤其是在他看来，这是与工作相关的

1513
01:13:02.180 --> 01:13:04.360
milestone for someone in his mind.
里程碑的一部分。

1514
01:13:04.500 --> 01:13:06.140
So it makes total sense we go to the beet farm.
所以去甜菜农场是完全合情合理的。

1515
01:13:06.140 --> 01:13:11.800
This we spent forever talking about what would and wouldn't happen and what camera angles
我们花了很长时间讨论什么会发生、什么不会发生，以及什么样的拍摄角度

1516
01:13:11.800 --> 01:13:14.120
would and wouldn't be possible.
是可行的，什么样的不可行。

1517
01:13:14.320 --> 01:13:16.340
And I don't think the audience cared at all.
但我认为观众根本不在乎这些。

1518
01:13:16.460 --> 01:13:22.020
I did my research and I spent 21 minutes and 40 seconds watching the episode last night.
我做了功课，昨晚花了21分40秒看完了这一集。

1519
01:13:22.540 --> 01:13:25.160
So in preparation for this podcaSt.
为了准备这次播客。

1520
01:13:25.560 --> 01:13:28.100
And it was just a joy to watch.
看这一集简直是一种享受。

1521
01:13:28.220 --> 01:13:31.460
But as I watched that, I was like, oh, this is Pam's episode.
但在看的时候，我就想，噢，这是帕姆的一集。

1522
01:13:31.460 --> 01:13:33.140
It's called The Initiation.
这一集叫《入会仪式》。

1523
01:13:33.460 --> 01:13:42.520
And yes, the flashy part is Dwight in the barn and the car and Ryan and the eggs and whatnot.
没错，最抢眼的部分是德怀特在谷仓、车里，还有瑞安和鸡蛋什么的。

1524
01:13:42.740 --> 01:13:50.700
But really, it's the heart and soul of this episode is Pam being told by Jan to spy on Michael.
但实际上，这一集的灵魂在于简让帕姆去监视迈克尔。

1525
01:13:52.300 --> 01:14:00.880
And then the exquisitely beautiful scene with Pam and Jim at the end that is by far the longest scene.
还有最后帕姆和吉姆那段极其优美的戏，那绝对是全剧最长的一场戏。

1526
01:14:01.100 --> 01:14:07.420
I mean, it must have been a five-page scene and had so much heart in it and subtlety.
我的意思是，那场戏足足有五页纸长，充满了温情和细腻的情感。

1527
01:14:07.740 --> 01:14:09.160
And that's...
而且那是……

1528
01:14:09.920 --> 01:14:13.700
So I'd love to hear the Pam perspective on this episode.
所以我很想听听帕姆对这一集的看法。

1529
01:14:14.040 --> 01:14:18.060
I had forgotten about that scene when I rewatched this episode.
重温这一集时，我都忘了还有那场戏了。

1530
01:14:18.060 --> 01:14:20.000
I forgot that happened at the end.
我忘了最后还有那一幕。

1531
01:14:20.280 --> 01:14:20.960
I did too.
我也是。

1532
01:14:21.220 --> 01:14:25.000
I held my breath and I was on the edge of my seat.
我屏住呼吸，紧张得坐在椅子边缘。

1533
01:14:25.280 --> 01:14:27.620
And I was like, what is happening?
当时我就想，到底发生了什么？

1534
01:14:27.980 --> 01:14:28.940
Don't get off the phone.
别挂电话。

1535
01:14:29.100 --> 01:14:29.780
Stay on the phone.
别挂电话。

1536
01:14:30.160 --> 01:14:31.240
Say feelings.
说出你的感受。

1537
01:14:31.480 --> 01:14:32.640
Say you miss him.
说你很想他。

1538
01:14:33.780 --> 01:14:36.060
You know, I'm just remembering...
你知道，我刚想起……

1539
01:14:37.220 --> 01:14:38.340
It's so funny, Rain.
真有意思，雷恩。

1540
01:14:38.380 --> 01:14:42.240
We were talking about the experimental episode because that card was on the board for a long time.
我们之前在讨论那个实验性剧集，因为那个点子在白板上挂了很久。

1541
01:14:42.500 --> 01:14:43.780
Jim and Pam's phone call.
就是吉姆和帕姆的通话。

1542
01:14:44.940 --> 01:14:47.480
And it was going to take the whole episode.
原本打算贯穿整集。

1543
01:14:47.480 --> 01:14:48.900
I fought so hard.
我当时极力争取。

1544
01:14:49.120 --> 01:14:50.920
I wanted it to be...
我希望它能……

1545
01:14:50.920 --> 01:14:53.860
Because it just happens at the end for a long time, right?
因为它只是在最后持续了很长时间，对吧？

1546
01:14:54.000 --> 01:14:54.820
The way we shot it.
我们拍摄的方式。

1547
01:14:54.980 --> 01:14:55.080
Yeah.
是的。

1548
01:14:55.180 --> 01:14:56.200
I wanted it to...
我希望它能……

1549
01:14:56.200 --> 01:14:59.960
You keep coming back to it and it's still going.
你不断地切回那个画面，而通话还在继续。

1550
01:15:00.140 --> 01:15:01.320
And it goes the whole episode.
它贯穿了整整一集。

1551
01:15:01.460 --> 01:15:02.520
They're on the phone the whole episode.
他们整集都在打电话。

1552
01:15:02.720 --> 01:15:09.800
In the DVD commentary, BJ, you mentioned that in your mind, this conversation went on for like three hours.
BJ，你在DVD评论音轨里提到过，在你看来，这段对话持续了大概三个小时。

1553
01:15:10.500 --> 01:15:11.640
Yeah, that sounds right.
没错，听起来确实如此。

1554
01:15:11.640 --> 01:15:13.980
I wanted it to be threaded through the episode.
我当时想把它贯穿整集。

1555
01:15:13.980 --> 01:15:21.060
And then I even wonder if I wanted it to be a whole episode at one point, their phone call, which is, again,
甚至有那么一刻，我还在想是不是该专门做一集关于他们通话的内容，这又一次，

1556
01:15:21.180 --> 01:15:27.820
in line with me and Rain's sort of experimental one-off outlier episode love.
符合我和雷恩对那种实验性、单集式、非典型剧集的偏爱。

1557
01:15:28.740 --> 01:15:30.000
But yeah, I remember that phone call.
不过确实，我记得那通电话。

1558
01:15:30.100 --> 01:15:34.780
And I remember writing the line, the one line I remember them proud of is, what time zone are you in?
我还记得写过一句台词，唯一一句让我感到自豪的是：你在哪个时区？

1559
01:15:35.080 --> 01:15:35.780
Same time zone.
同一个时区。

1560
01:15:35.860 --> 01:15:36.700
Oh, it felt far.
哦，感觉好遥远。

1561
01:15:36.800 --> 01:15:37.900
I was like, yes, of course.
我当时就想，对，当然了。

1562
01:15:38.180 --> 01:15:39.660
Oh, beautiful line.
哦，绝妙的台词。

1563
01:15:39.800 --> 01:15:40.400
Yeah, that got me.
是啊，那句打动了我。

1564
01:15:40.400 --> 01:15:46.320
In watching this episode, I was like, oh, this is why this show has stood the test of time.
在看这一集的时候，我心想，哦，这就是这部剧能经受住时间考验的原因。

1565
01:15:46.660 --> 01:15:52.920
Because you have scenes that are outrageously over the top.
因为你既有那些极其夸张的场景。

1566
01:15:52.960 --> 01:16:01.400
And then all of a sudden, it's two people in love that hardly know they're in love having, you know,
然后突然间，又是两个深陷爱河却几乎没意识到自己坠入爱河的人，进行着，你知道，

1567
01:16:01.480 --> 01:16:07.340
an almost unedited five-minute conversation that it's almost like it's in real time.
一段几乎未经剪辑的五分钟对话，感觉就像是实时发生的一样。

1568
01:16:07.340 --> 01:16:14.440
And you have this moment of, like, real heart underneath it that grounds that whole experience.
而且你会在其中感受到那种真实的内心触动，为整个体验奠定了基调。

1569
01:16:14.960 --> 01:16:22.900
And I always love that Greg talked about having that, you know, a show can't support more than, like, 10% or 15% hearts.
我一直很喜欢格雷格谈论的那种观点，你知道，一部剧不能承载超过10%或15%的真情实感。

1570
01:16:23.040 --> 01:16:26.920
It's got to have 80%, 85% comedy in it to work.
它必须包含80%到85%的喜剧成分才能奏效。

1571
01:16:26.920 --> 01:16:34.580
But you can't leave out that 10%, 15% of reality, or else you'll have lost the audience.
但你不能丢掉那10%到15%的现实感，否则你就会失去观众。

1572
01:16:34.820 --> 01:16:36.160
Greg was good with percentages.
格雷格很擅长把控这些比例。

1573
01:16:36.160 --> 01:16:46.940
He also had the 5% rule, which was that every character, you should try to move them forward 5%, surprise them 5%.
他还有个“5%原则”，就是说对于每个角色，你应该尝试让他们进步5%，给他们带来5%的惊喜。

1574
01:16:46.940 --> 01:16:57.400
If a character is always exactly what you expect, it gets, you know, boring and you fall into cliched ideas of what Angela would do or whatever.
如果一个角色总是完全符合你的预期，那就会变得，你知道，很无聊，你会陷入对安吉拉会做什么之类的刻板印象中。

1575
01:16:57.400 --> 01:17:08.280
But, and if you change it by 50% or 100%, if all of a sudden Michael has read the complete Shakespeare, it's funny, but it's, you killed the character.
但是，如果你改变了50%或100%，比如迈克尔突然读完了莎士比亚全集，这虽然好笑，但你毁了这个角色。

1576
01:17:08.280 --> 01:17:12.160
So it's, you always want to be like, huh, all right, I kind of see that.
所以，你总是希望观众觉得，嗯，好吧，我大概能理解。

1577
01:17:12.580 --> 01:17:17.680
So, yeah, that's just Greg with, if he, I didn't never heard him give that percentage, but that sounds like Greg, it sounds right.
所以，是的，这就是格雷格的风格，如果他……我从没听他亲口说过这个百分比，但这听起来很像格雷格，听起来很对。

1578
01:17:17.840 --> 01:17:18.900
I just have a question, Rain.
我有个问题，雷恩。

1579
01:17:18.900 --> 01:17:29.300
I mean, when Ryan comes up to the barn, you do this salute, and people online think it's like you sort of like, sort of imitating the salute from a BBC show called,
我是说，当瑞安走到谷仓时，你行了一个军礼，网友们觉得你是在模仿一部BBC剧集里的军礼，

1580
01:17:29.300 --> 01:17:31.020
it's called Red Dwarf.
那部剧叫《红矮星号》。

1581
01:17:32.480 --> 01:17:36.740
Is that, is that from Red Dwarf, the BBC show from the 80s?
那是来自《红矮星号》吗，那部80年代的BBC剧集？

1582
01:17:36.840 --> 01:17:46.560
I don't remember how that came out, but I, I, my hunch is that in the script, and you can tell me, Dwight does a strange salute or something like that,
我不记得那是怎么来的了，但我，我的直觉是剧本里写着，你可以告诉我，德怀特做了一个奇怪的军礼之类的，

1583
01:17:46.600 --> 01:17:49.480
so I had to kind of come up with what that was.
所以我不得不自己想出那是什么样的动作。

1584
01:17:49.800 --> 01:17:56.080
Maybe that's not in the script, I don't know, you can research that, but I, I don't know what that was, but I, I like that it's kind of like,
也许剧本里没写，我不知道，你可以去查查，但我，我不知道那是什么，但我喜欢它那种，

1585
01:17:56.860 --> 01:18:03.100
uh, World War I Germany, kind of like the Kaiser, like that's how you would salute the Kaiser.
呃，一战时期的德国，有点像凯撒，就像那是你向凯撒敬礼的方式。

1586
01:18:03.400 --> 01:18:17.160
Can I point out, I'm realizing this is not our first writer-actor collaboration, where I write a stage direction for Dwight that he makes iconic, which is, I remember in The Fire.
我可以指出一点吗？我意识到这已经不是我们第一次进行编剧与演员的合作了，我为德怀特写了一个舞台指示，结果被他演成了经典，我记得是在《火灾》那一集。

1587
01:18:17.380 --> 01:18:18.500
Yes, I do it.
是的，我记得。

1588
01:18:18.520 --> 01:18:18.940
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

1589
01:18:19.320 --> 01:18:24.600
In The Fire, I wrote, the fire truck arrives, and Dwight pumps his fiSt.
在《火灾》里，我写道：消防车到了，德怀特挥舞拳头。

1590
01:18:25.300 --> 01:18:26.800
And I think Greg was like, huh?
我想格雷格当时问：啊？

1591
01:18:26.940 --> 01:18:30.560
And I was like, no, he's like a little boy, he just sees a fire truck, and he's like, yeah!
我说：不，他就像个小男孩，看到消防车就兴奋地喊：耶！

1592
01:18:32.760 --> 01:18:38.700
And you did it, and it's great, and now it's like a GIF or something, it's like a meme, it's just, it's exactly what I dreamed of.
你做到了，效果很棒，现在它成了GIF图或者表情包之类的，这正是我梦寐以求的效果。

1593
01:18:38.900 --> 01:18:48.720
And I think, on that, you know, we had like, eight takes or something, so at first it was like, standard fist pump, and then it got bigger and bigger until finally at the end,
我想，在那场戏里，我们拍了大概八次，所以起初只是标准的挥拳，然后动作越来越大，直到最后，

1594
01:18:48.860 --> 01:18:49.580
it's like, yeah!
变成了：耶！

1595
01:18:52.600 --> 01:18:55.040
Oh my god, DJ is so tickled.
天哪，BJ被逗乐了。

1596
01:18:55.260 --> 01:19:04.120
I'm just laughing at how much Dwight loved, it's a toaster oven, like with a little bit of smoke, and he sees a fire truck, and he's like, yes!
我只是在笑德怀特有多喜欢，那只是个烤箱，冒了一点烟，他看到消防车就觉得：太棒了！

1597
01:19:08.100 --> 01:19:10.400
This is such an excessive solution!
这反应也太夸张了！

1598
01:19:13.460 --> 01:19:21.080
Although I suppose that's what happens when the alarm goes off, they just come, but it's just like, he would think this is appropriate as opposed to annoying!
虽然我想警报响了他们确实会来，但他居然会觉得这很合适，而不是觉得烦人！

1599
01:19:26.480 --> 01:19:27.340
Alright, alright.
好吧，好吧。

1600
01:19:27.780 --> 01:19:32.120
Yeah, it would, for Dwight, it ranks in like, his top ten best days ever.
是啊，对德怀特来说，这能排进他人生中最棒的前十天。

1601
01:19:32.400 --> 01:19:40.240
Like, if he was making a journal, like, Dear Diary, best days ever, number four, fire truck showed up to Dunder Mifflin.
就像他在写日记一样，亲爱的日记，有史以来最棒的日子，第四天，消防车出现在了邓德·米夫林公司。

1602
01:19:40.960 --> 01:19:47.780
Another thing I improvised in this episode was, in the barn, going back to the barn now, the thing of like, Moe's, where are all the animals?
这一集里我即兴发挥的另一件事是，在谷仓里，回到谷仓那场戏，关于莫斯，所有的动物都去哪了？

1603
01:19:48.540 --> 01:19:50.600
Yes, I was gonna ask you that, Ray!
没错，我正想问你呢，雷！

1604
01:19:50.880 --> 01:19:51.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1605
01:19:51.520 --> 01:19:53.420
I love that line so much!
我太喜欢那句台词了！

1606
01:19:53.420 --> 01:20:02.840
But we were laughing, BJ and I, about it on the set, and just kind of like, we didn't quite know how to, I don't know that it ultimately landed as a joke,
但我和BJ在片场时一直在笑，我们当时不太确定该怎么处理，不知道最终呈现出来的效果算不算个笑话，

1607
01:20:02.980 --> 01:20:09.160
but the idea that there should have been, it should have been filled with animals, but now it was empty of animals.
但那个想法是，那里本该挤满了动物，但现在却空空如也。

1608
01:20:09.360 --> 01:20:11.220
So what did Moe's do with all the animals?
所以莫斯把那些动物都弄哪去了？

1609
01:20:11.360 --> 01:20:12.100
Where did he put them?
他把它们放哪了？

1610
01:20:12.240 --> 01:20:14.640
He probably brought them and put them in the house.
他大概把它们带回屋里去了。

1611
01:20:14.840 --> 01:20:17.420
And that, that might have been a nice cutaway.
那可能是一个不错的切入镜头。

1612
01:20:17.420 --> 01:20:18.720
He's like, Moe's, where's all the animals?
他当时说，莫斯，所有的动物都去哪了？

1613
01:20:18.860 --> 01:20:26.160
And then just cut away to Dwight's actual house with a, filled with cows and sheep and pigs and chickens and whatnot.
然后直接切到德怀特真正的家里，里面挤满了牛、羊、猪、鸡之类的动物。

1614
01:20:27.140 --> 01:20:30.020
Speaking of this scene, can I play an audio clip from this scene?
说到这场戏，我能放一段这场戏的音频片段吗？

1615
01:20:30.240 --> 01:20:36.600
I asked Sam to pull this audio clip from when Dwight is rapid fire questioning Ryan.
我让萨姆找来了德怀特连珠炮式质问瑞安的那段音频。

1616
01:20:37.980 --> 01:20:39.300
Can you play that clip, Sam?
萨姆，能播放一下那个片段吗？

1617
01:20:39.300 --> 01:20:43.880
What is the greatest danger facing Dunder Mifflin?
邓德·米夫林面临的最大危险是什么？

1618
01:20:43.980 --> 01:20:46.260
Outsourcing and consolidation of competition.
外包和竞争对手的合并。

1619
01:20:46.500 --> 01:20:46.780
Wrong.
错。

1620
01:20:47.100 --> 01:20:47.900
Flash floods.
山洪暴发。

1621
01:20:48.420 --> 01:20:53.300
What is the true cause of Robert Mifflin's suicide?
罗伯特·米夫林自杀的真正原因是什么？

1622
01:20:54.760 --> 01:20:55.660
Depression.
抑郁症。

1623
01:20:56.000 --> 01:20:56.280
Wrong.
错。

1624
01:20:56.440 --> 01:20:57.180
He hated himself.
他厌恶自己。

1625
01:20:57.820 --> 01:20:59.920
What is the Dharma Initiative?
达摩计划是什么？

1626
01:21:00.620 --> 01:21:04.440
Final question, young Ryan Howard.
最后一个问题，年轻的瑞安·霍华德。

1627
01:21:04.940 --> 01:21:08.620
What is Michael Scott's?
迈克尔·斯科特最大的恐惧是什么？

1628
01:21:09.400 --> 01:21:10.300
Greatest fear.
最大的恐惧。

1629
01:21:12.060 --> 01:21:13.180
Um, loneliness.
嗯，孤独。

1630
01:21:16.000 --> 01:21:16.820
Maybe women.
也许是女人。

1631
01:21:17.200 --> 01:21:17.520
Wrong.
错。

1632
01:21:18.380 --> 01:21:19.680
He's not afraid of anything.
他什么都不怕。

1633
01:21:20.700 --> 01:21:22.800
Also, I would have accepted snakes.
另外，如果回答蛇的话我也能接受。

1634
01:21:23.440 --> 01:21:25.700
I believe Justin Spitzer wrote that pitch.
我相信这个点子是贾斯汀·斯皮策写的。

1635
01:21:25.900 --> 01:21:31.780
Justin Spitzer, uh, in the writer's room, you know, you send writers off sometimes to just like,
贾斯汀·斯皮策，呃，在编剧室里，你知道，有时候你会让编剧们去，

1636
01:21:31.860 --> 01:21:33.240
all right, you write a bunch of questions.
好了，你们去写一堆问题。

1637
01:21:33.460 --> 01:21:35.160
You, you and you write this scene.
你，你，还有你，去写这场戏。

1638
01:21:35.300 --> 01:21:38.680
And I, I remember Justin coming back with some really good stuff.
我记得贾斯汀回来时带了一些非常棒的内容。

1639
01:21:38.680 --> 01:21:41.200
And I think he wrote loneliness, which I loved.
我想他写了孤独，我非常喜欢。

1640
01:21:41.440 --> 01:21:44.080
But then you said, or maybe fear of women.
但后来你说，或者也许是害怕女人。

1641
01:21:44.340 --> 01:21:44.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1642
01:21:44.720 --> 01:21:45.640
Who put maybe women?
谁加了也许是女人？

1643
01:21:45.940 --> 01:21:46.140
Oh.
哦。

1644
01:21:46.400 --> 01:21:49.360
Loneliness was your first take on Michael's greatest fear.
孤独是你对迈克尔最大恐惧的第一反应。

1645
01:21:49.660 --> 01:21:51.740
And then you say, or maybe women.
然后你说，或者也许是女人。

1646
01:21:52.120 --> 01:21:54.880
And then Dwight is like false, but I would accept snakes.
然后德怀特说错误，但我会接受蛇这个答案。

1647
01:21:55.300 --> 01:21:56.980
He's not afraid of anything.
他什么都不怕。

1648
01:21:57.720 --> 01:21:59.660
But I would have accepted snakes.
但我本来会接受蛇这个答案的。

1649
01:22:00.520 --> 01:22:00.900
Right.
没错。

1650
01:22:02.940 --> 01:22:04.100
What a loyaliSt.
真是个忠诚的人。

1651
01:22:04.620 --> 01:22:06.900
But guys, this is the scene that introduces Moe's.
但伙计们，这可是莫斯登场的那个场景。

1652
01:22:07.000 --> 01:22:08.340
We were talking about Moe's.
我们当时在聊莫斯。

1653
01:22:08.460 --> 01:22:09.180
And Mike Schur.
还有迈克·舒尔。

1654
01:22:09.640 --> 01:22:11.100
How did that come about?
那是怎么定下来的？

1655
01:22:11.300 --> 01:22:12.560
Everyone wants to know.
大家都想知道。

1656
01:22:13.520 --> 01:22:17.960
Mike did an interview where he said that's his real beard and it took him three months to grow.
迈克在一次采访中说那是他真实的胡子，留了三个月才长成那样。

1657
01:22:18.500 --> 01:22:20.220
Wait, all of that underneath?
等等，下面全是那种胡子？

1658
01:22:20.220 --> 01:22:20.980
That was just hilarious.
那简直太搞笑了。

1659
01:22:21.680 --> 01:22:23.040
That was his hair?
那是他自己的头发？

1660
01:22:23.280 --> 01:22:24.920
Yeah, that's his real hair.
对，那是他真实的胡子。

1661
01:22:25.280 --> 01:22:26.240
Oh my God.
天哪。

1662
01:22:26.880 --> 01:22:33.060
What an, like, I thought I had it hard having to wear cheesy blonde highlights for six months.
真是……我原本以为自己为了角色戴六个月俗气的金色挑染已经够惨了。

1663
01:22:33.060 --> 01:22:38.940
But Moe's, Mike, had to wear a neckbeard.
但莫斯，也就是迈克，得留着那种颈须。

1664
01:22:39.120 --> 01:22:41.040
And again, it's only a neckbeard.
而且再说一遍，那只是颈须。

1665
01:22:41.260 --> 01:22:44.900
And he's like a classy dude, you know?
他可是个体面人，你知道吧？

1666
01:22:45.180 --> 01:22:46.220
He's married.
他结婚了。

1667
01:22:46.220 --> 01:22:48.980
He's, you know, a TV producer.
他是个电视制作人。

1668
01:22:48.980 --> 01:22:49.940
People know him.
大家都认识他。

1669
01:22:49.940 --> 01:22:51.620
He has social engagements.
他有各种社交活动。

1670
01:22:51.700 --> 01:22:53.520
He's walking around with his neckbeard.
他却得顶着那副颈须到处走。

1671
01:22:53.760 --> 01:22:57.700
The thick neckbeard for months and months and months.
那浓密的颈须留了整整好几个月。

1672
01:22:57.700 --> 01:23:09.020
And this nothing made Greg Daniels happier or more amused than what Mike had to go through as sort of, you know, supervising producer of The Office.
格雷格·丹尼尔斯对此乐此不疲，看着迈克作为《办公室》的监制却不得不经历这些，让他觉得特别好笑。

1673
01:23:09.200 --> 01:23:11.680
And yet he also had to wear this neckbeard.
然而他还是得留着那副颈须。

1674
01:23:11.780 --> 01:23:13.460
He never asked to act.
他从没主动要求演戏。

1675
01:23:15.340 --> 01:23:22.740
And the funniest part of it is that Mike kept asking, don't you think we could just use a fake beard?
最搞笑的是，迈克一直问，难道我们就不能用假胡子吗？

1676
01:23:23.560 --> 01:23:26.020
And Greg said, no, absolutely not.
格雷格说，不行，绝对不行。

1677
01:23:26.020 --> 01:23:27.300
People will tell the difference.
观众一眼就能看出来。

1678
01:23:27.700 --> 01:23:34.560
And then, I don't know what the reason was, but maybe it was, like, we suddenly came back from, you know, a long hiatus.
后来，我不知道具体原因，可能是因为我们刚从漫长的休假中回来。

1679
01:23:34.740 --> 01:23:37.180
And a rewrite had to throw Moe's in a scene.
剧本重写时临时加了一场莫斯的戏。

1680
01:23:37.200 --> 01:23:38.080
He didn't have the beard.
他当时没留胡子。

1681
01:23:38.260 --> 01:23:41.120
And we just threw a $5 fake beard on.
于是我们随便贴了个五美元的假胡子上去。

1682
01:23:41.260 --> 01:23:42.720
It was indistinguishable.
根本看不出区别。

1683
01:23:43.040 --> 01:23:43.700
And it was totally fine.
效果完全没问题。

1684
01:23:44.540 --> 01:23:45.380
Totally fine.
完全没问题。

1685
01:23:45.520 --> 01:23:51.640
Now, how did they decide Mike Schur was going to play his Amish farmer cousin?
那么，他们是怎么决定让迈克·舒尔去演他那位阿米什农民表亲的？

1686
01:23:51.640 --> 01:23:57.620
Yeah, it was, I think it was, it was, I'm 60% confident.
嗯，我觉得，我有六成把握。

1687
01:23:57.620 --> 01:23:58.940
It was a room bit.
那是编剧室里的一个梗。

1688
01:23:59.240 --> 01:24:05.140
I think Mike did the voice in sort of a never thinking it would lead to anything.
我觉得迈克当时只是随口模仿了那个口音，根本没想过会有下文。

1689
01:24:05.260 --> 01:24:10.260
There's a lot of room bits where you're just joking around for hours, cracking each other up as a way of warming up.
编剧室里有很多这种梗，大家只是为了热身，聚在一起胡侃几个小时，互相逗乐。

1690
01:24:10.260 --> 01:24:11.660
And maybe it leads to something, who knows?
也许这会引出什么后续，谁知道呢？

1691
01:24:11.800 --> 01:24:12.420
It's just goofing off.
纯粹是闹着玩。

1692
01:24:12.580 --> 01:24:15.100
And I think as a room bit, he did that voice.
我觉得就是因为那个梗，他才用了那种口音。

1693
01:24:15.880 --> 01:24:18.460
And maybe that's what cracked Greg up and made him think.
可能正是这点戳中了格雷格的笑点，让他动了心思。

1694
01:24:18.640 --> 01:24:20.160
So then we took the picture.
于是我们就拍了那张照片。

1695
01:24:20.580 --> 01:24:24.820
But I think the idea was always, someday we'll see Moe's nudge, nudge.
但我觉得大家一直以来的想法都是，总有一天我们会让莫斯登场，你懂的。

1696
01:24:25.360 --> 01:24:27.880
But like, we didn't even know if we'd be picked up, you know?
但当时我们甚至不知道剧集会不会被续订，你明白吗？

1697
01:24:28.040 --> 01:24:32.580
But I do think it was, I do think it was assumed that he would play Moe's if it ever happened.
不过我确实认为，大家默认如果真有那一天，肯定是由他来演莫斯。

1698
01:24:33.640 --> 01:24:36.720
We have a fan question from Quinn Moldenhauer.
我们有一个来自奎因·莫尔登豪尔的粉丝提问。

1699
01:24:37.640 --> 01:24:38.000
Finally.
终于来了。

1700
01:24:38.880 --> 01:24:40.620
Yes, he would like to know.
没错，他想知道的是。

1701
01:24:42.500 --> 01:24:46.160
What would have happened if Ryan had actually gotten in the coffin?
如果瑞安真的进了棺材，会发生什么？

1702
01:24:46.440 --> 01:24:47.460
What were you going to do?
你们打算做什么？

1703
01:24:47.580 --> 01:24:49.980
Were you going to bury him next to your grandfather?
你们打算把他埋在你祖父旁边吗？

1704
01:24:50.020 --> 01:24:50.960
What was going to happen?
到底会发生什么？

1705
01:24:51.020 --> 01:24:52.520
Yeah, he was going to put a padlock.
没错，他打算装一把挂锁。

1706
01:24:52.700 --> 01:24:54.580
He was going to put a padlock on the coffin.
他打算在棺材上装一把挂锁。

1707
01:24:54.820 --> 01:25:00.040
They were going to wheel it via donkey cart out to the Shruth Cemetery.
他们打算用驴车把它运到斯鲁斯公墓。

1708
01:25:00.280 --> 01:25:02.040
And they were going to bury him.
然后他们打算把他埋了。

1709
01:25:02.760 --> 01:25:14.000
And they're going to, and he's going to, Moe's was going to dress up like a chaplain and do a eulogy so that Ryan had a taste of death.
他们打算，他打算，莫打算装扮成牧师做悼词，好让瑞安体验一下死亡的感觉。

1710
01:25:14.560 --> 01:25:16.600
And then the sweetness of life.
然后体验生命的甜美。

1711
01:25:16.780 --> 01:25:18.560
And then they would bury him.
接着他们会把他埋了。

1712
01:25:19.040 --> 01:25:23.980
Dwight would rescue him and bring the coffin up, throw the dirt off the coffin, undo the padlock,
德怀特会去救他，把棺材抬上来，把棺材上的土扫掉，解开挂锁，

1713
01:25:23.980 --> 01:25:24.940
open it up.
打开它。

1714
01:25:25.060 --> 01:25:26.920
Ryan would be like, what the fuck, Dwight?
瑞安会说，搞什么鬼，德怀特？

1715
01:25:27.040 --> 01:25:29.080
And Dwight would be like, I rescued you, Ryan.
德怀特会说，我救了你，瑞安。

1716
01:25:29.220 --> 01:25:29.840
I rescued you.
我救了你。

1717
01:25:30.060 --> 01:25:30.420
Welcome.
不客气。

1718
01:25:30.520 --> 01:25:31.060
You're alive.
你还活着。

1719
01:25:31.060 --> 01:25:31.740
You made it.
你挺过来了。

1720
01:25:31.840 --> 01:25:32.140
You're alive.
你还活着。

1721
01:25:32.140 --> 01:25:32.880
You're reborn.
你重生了。

1722
01:25:33.480 --> 01:25:34.200
You're reborn.
你重生了。

1723
01:25:34.320 --> 01:25:36.140
You're reborn as a Dunder Mifflin.
你作为邓德·米夫林的一员重生了。

1724
01:25:36.220 --> 01:25:37.320
And I saved you.
而我救了你。

1725
01:25:37.320 --> 01:25:40.620
And then that this would be a profound experience.
然后这会是一次深刻的体验。

1726
01:25:42.420 --> 01:25:43.280
That sounds right.
听起来很有道理。

1727
01:25:43.760 --> 01:25:44.680
I like that.
我喜欢这个主意。

1728
01:25:45.320 --> 01:25:47.140
Quinn will be very happy to hear.
奎因听到会很高兴的。

1729
01:25:47.340 --> 01:25:50.460
On that note, I'm going to move us along to Axelrod Limited.
说到这，我要带大家进入下一个话题：阿克塞尔罗德有限公司。

1730
01:25:51.380 --> 01:25:51.820
Please.
请讲。

1731
01:25:51.820 --> 01:25:54.460
We find out that they didn't like Ryan.
我们发现他们不喜欢瑞安。

1732
01:25:54.700 --> 01:25:56.100
They didn't make the sale.
他们没做成那笔生意。

1733
01:25:56.820 --> 01:26:01.120
Rain, you have that great line where you're like, I mean, they didn't need to say it to your face.
雷恩，你有一句很棒的台词，大概是说，我是说，他们没必要当面说出来。

1734
01:26:01.880 --> 01:26:03.100
But they didn't like you.
但他们就是不喜欢你。

1735
01:26:03.640 --> 01:26:05.180
It's a really great line.
那真是一句很棒的台词。

1736
01:26:06.160 --> 01:26:07.140
It's really great.
真的很棒。

1737
01:26:07.380 --> 01:26:10.120
But so then you guys end up egging the building.
但后来你们去朝那栋楼扔鸡蛋了。

1738
01:26:10.900 --> 01:26:16.000
We had a fan question from Chandra who wants to know, did you throw real eggs at the building?
我们收到一个粉丝钱德拉的问题，她想知道，你们当时扔的是真鸡蛋吗？

1739
01:26:16.600 --> 01:26:17.480
Do you guys remember?
你们还记得吗？

1740
01:26:17.700 --> 01:26:17.860
Yes.
记得。

1741
01:26:18.000 --> 01:26:25.140
So the Axelrod sign that's hanging up on the side of the building was a fabrication from our art department.
挂在楼侧面的阿克塞尔罗德招牌是我们美术部门制作的道具。

1742
01:26:25.340 --> 01:26:26.720
And they hung it up there.
他们把它挂在那里。

1743
01:26:26.840 --> 01:26:27.760
And that was our target.
那就是我们的目标。

1744
01:26:28.560 --> 01:26:31.980
And, you know, we had worked out with the building itself.
而且，你知道，我们和那栋楼的负责人协商好了。

1745
01:26:31.980 --> 01:26:35.020
Like, we had a pressure hose right there.
比如，我们就在那儿准备了高压水枪。

1746
